// Deviates from a straight Explosion mapping: CharacterAbility::Explosion
// (common/src/states/explosion.rs) always detonates centered on the
// caster's own position -- it has no target-point field at all, only a
// `radius`. This spell's own sheet range (18 m, thrown at a chosen point)
// contradicts that, so it uses GroundAoe instead, the engine's real
// "detonate at a chosen point within range" primitive (see
// assets/common/abilities/spells/axiomancy/dark_star.ron for the sibling
// shape this was cloned from).
//
// Also note: GroundAoe hardcodes DamageKind::Energy in
// common/src/states/ground_aoe.rs (no RON-configurable damage_kind field
// exists on this variant) -- so despite the Acid flavor text, this deals
// generic Energy damage under the hood. Same category of engine-vs-flavor
// drift as this batch's melee spells; noted, not hidden.
//
// Damage is set below the batch's single-target cantrip baseline (14),
// same AoE-cantrip discount as thunderclap.ron/word_of_radiance.ron: this
// can hit everyone caught in the burst radius, not just one target,
// matching real D&D's own Acid Splash die (1d6, below Fire Bolt's 1d10).
GroundAoe(
    energy_cost: 0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    delay: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    max_range: 18.0,
    radius: 3.0,
    min_falloff: 0.3,
    damage: 10,
    poise: 5,
    knockback: (strength: 0, direction: Away),
    dodgeable: Roll,
    rooted_cast: false,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
